{\"input\":[{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"input_text\",\"text\":\"\\nTASK: Optimize the following Triton kernel based on hardware profiling analysis to achieve better performance.\\n\\n## TARGET GPU\\n- GPU: AMD Instinct MI300X\\n- Architecture: CDNA3 (gfx942)\\n- Peak Memory Bandwidth: 5300.0 GB/s\\n- Peak FP32: 163.0 TFLOPS\\n- Peak FP16: 1300.0 TFLOPS\\n- Peak BF16: 1300.0 TFLOPS\\n- SM Count: 304\\n- Max Threads per SM: 2048\\n- L1 Cache per SM: 32 KB\\n- L2 Cache: 4 MB\\n- Memory: 192 GB HBM3\\n\\n## PROBLEM DESCRIPTION\\nimport torch\\nimport torch.nn as nn\\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\\nimport os\\n\\n\\nclass Model(nn.Module):\\n    def __init__(self):\\n        super(Model, self).__init__()\\n\\n    def forward(self, Q: torch.Tensor, K: torch.Tensor, V: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\\n        if K.shape[1] == 1:\\n            K = K.repeat_interleave(8, dim=1)\\n            V = V.repeat_interleave(8, dim=1)\\n\\n        return F.scaled_dot_product_attention(\\n            Q, K, V, attn_mask=None, dropout_p=0.0, is_causal=True\\n        )\\n\\n\\nbatch_size = 16\\nnum_q_heads = 8\\nnum_kv_heads = 1\\nsequence_length = int(os.getenv(\\\"ATTN_SEQ_LEN\\\", \\\"1024\\\"))\\nhead_dim = 128\\nsupported_sequence_lengths = (1024, 2048, 4096, 8192, 16384)\\n\\n\\ndef get_inputs():\\n    Q = torch.randn(batch_size, num_q_heads, sequence_length, head_dim, dtype=torch.bfloat16)\\n    K = torch.randn(batch_size, num_kv_heads, sequence_length, head_dim, dtype=torch.bfloat16)\\n    V = torch.randn(batch_size, num_kv_heads, sequence_length, head_dim, dtype=torch.bfloat16)\\n    return [Q, K, V]\\n\\n\\ndef get_init_inputs():\\n    return []\\n\\nPyTorch Eager baseline: 0.2918 ms\\n\\n## CURRENT KERNEL\\n```python\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nTriton implementation of causal scaled dot-product attention for the test contract.\\n\\nFused stages in a single Triton kernel:\\n1) QK^T block matmul (streamed over K dimension)\\n2) Causal masking\\n3) Numerically stable online softmax (max/sum update)\\n4) PV matmul accumulation\\n5) Final normalization and output store\\n\\nNotes:\\n- Supports the exact test pattern: Q=[B, Hq, S, D], K/V=[B, Hkv, S, D] with Hkv in {1, Hq}\\n- If Hkv == 1, kernel performs grouped-query attention by mapping all query heads to kv-head 0.\\n- No torch.nn / torch.nn.functional / torch compute ops are used for math.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nimport torch\\nimport triton\\nimport triton.language as tl\\n\\n\\n@triton.jit\\ndef _fused_causal_attention_kernel(\\n    q_ptr, k_ptr, v_ptr, o_ptr,\\n    B, HQ, HKV, S, D,\\n    stride_qb, stride_qh, stride_qs, stride_qd,\\n    stride_kb, stride_kh, stride_ks, stride_kd,\\n    stride_vb, stride_vh, stride_vs, stride_vd,\\n    stride_ob, stride_oh, stride_os, stride_od,\\n    scale,\\n    BLOCK_M: tl.constexpr,\\n    BLOCK_N: tl.constexpr,\\n    BLOCK_D: tl.constexpr,\\n):\\n    pid_m = tl.program_id(0)  # sequence tile\\n    pid_bh = tl.program_id(1)  # batch * q_head\\n\\n    b = pid_bh // HQ\\n    hq = pid_bh % HQ\\n\\n    # GQA mapping: if HKV==1 map all q-heads -> kv-head 0 else one-to-one\\n    hkv = tl.where(HKV == 1, 0, hq)\\n\\n    offs_m = pid_m * BLOCK_M + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_M)\\n    offs_d = tl.arange(0, BLOCK_D)\\n\\n    q_ptrs = (\\n        q_ptr\\n        + b * stride_qb\\n        + hq * stride_qh\\n        + offs_m[:, None] * stride_qs\\n        + offs_d[None, :] * stride_qd\\n    )\\n    q_mask = (offs_m[:, None] < S) & (offs_d[None, :] < D)\\n    q = tl.load(q_ptrs, mask=q_mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\\n\\n    m_i = tl.full((BLOCK_M,), -float(\\\"inf\\\"), dtype=tl.float32)\\n    l_i = tl.zeros((BLOCK_M,), dtype=tl.float32)\\n    acc = tl.zeros((BLOCK_M, BLOCK_D), dtype=tl.float32)\\n\\n    n_start = 0\\n    while n_start < S:\\n        offs_n = n_start + tl.arange(0, BLOCK_N)\\n\\n        k_ptrs = (\\n            k_ptr\\n            + b * stride_kb\\n            + hkv * stride_kh\\n            + offs_n[:, None] * stride_ks\\n            + offs_d[None, :] * stride_kd\\n        )\\n        k_mask = (offs_n[:, None] < S) & (offs_d[None, :] < D)\\n        k = tl.load(k_ptrs, mask=k_mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\\n\\n        qk = tl.dot(q, tl.trans(k)) * scale\\n\\n        causal = offs_m[:, None] >= offs_n[None, :]\\n        valid_n = offs_n[None, :] < S\\n        qk = tl.where(causal & valid_n, qk, -1.0e9)\\n\\n        m_ij = tl.maximum(m_i, tl.max(qk, axis=1))\\n        p = tl.exp(qk - m_ij[:, None])\\n        l_ij = tl.sum(p, axis=1)\\n\\n        alpha = tl.exp(m_i - m_ij)\\n        l_i = l_i * alpha + l_ij\\n        acc = acc * alpha[:, None]\\n\\n        v_ptrs = (\\n            v_ptr\\n            + b * stride_vb\\n            + hkv * stride_vh\\n            + offs_n[:, None] * stride_vs\\n            + offs_d[None, :] * stride_vd\\n        )\\n        v_mask = (offs_n[:, None] < S) & (offs_d[None, :] < D)\\n        v = tl.load(v_ptrs, mask=v_mask, other=0.0).to(tl.float32)\\n\\n        acc = tl.dot(p.to(v.dtype), v, acc)\\n        m_i = m_ij\\n        n_start += BLOCK_N\\n\\n    out = acc / l_i[:, None]\\n\\n    o_ptrs = (\\n        o_ptr\\n        + b * stride_ob\\n        + hq * stride_oh\\n        + offs_m[:, None] * stride_os\\n        + offs_d[None, :] * stride_od\\n    )\\n    o_mask = (offs_m[:, None] < S) & (offs_d[None, :] < D)\\n    tl.store(o_ptrs, out.to(o_ptr.dtype.element_ty), mask=o_mask)\\n\\n\\ndef kernel_function(Q: torch.Tensor, K: torch.Tensor, V: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Wrapper: validates inputs, allocates output, launches fused Triton attention kernel.\\n\\n    Fusion rationale:\\n    - Entire attention forward pass is fused into one kernel launch per (batch, q_head, seq_tile):\\n      score matmul + causal mask + softmax + value matmul + writeback.\\n    - This avoids materializing attention matrices in global memory.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    assert Q.is_hip and K.is_hip and V.is_hip, \\\"Inputs must be on GPU\\\"\\n    assert Q.dtype == torch.bfloat16 and K.dtype == torch.bfloat16 and V.dtype == torch.bfloat16\\n    assert Q.ndim == 4 and K.ndim == 4 and V.ndim == 4\\n\\n    B, HQ, S, D = Q.shape\\n    BK, HKV, SK, DK = K.shape\\n    BV, HKV2, SV, DV = V.shape\\n\\n    assert B == BK == BV\\n    assert S == SK == SV\\n    assert D == DK == DV\\n    assert HKV == HKV2\\n    assert HKV == 1 or HKV == HQ\\n    assert D == 128  # matches test requirement\\n\\n    O = torch.empty_like(Q)\\n    scale = 1.0 / (D ** 0.5)\\n\\n    BLOCK_M = 64\\n    BLOCK_N = 64\\n    BLOCK_D = 128\\n\\n    grid = (triton.cdiv(S, BLOCK_M), B * HQ)\\n\\n    _fused_causal_attention_kernel[grid](\\n        Q, K, V, O,\\n        B, HQ, HKV, S, D,\\n        Q.stride(0), Q.stride(1), Q.stride(2), Q.stride(3),\\n        K.stride(0), K.stride(1), K.stride(2), K.stride(3),\\n        V.stride(0), V.stride(1), V.stride(2), V.stride(3),\\n        O.stride(0), O.stride(1), O.stride(2), O.stride(3),\\n        scale,\\n        BLOCK_M=BLOCK_M,\\n        BLOCK_N=BLOCK_N,\\n        BLOCK_D=BLOCK_D,\\n        num_warps=8,\\n        num_stages=2,\\n    )\\n    return O\\n```\\n\\n## ROOFLINE ANALYSIS\\n- Primary Bottleneck: COMPUTE\\n- Compute SOL: 92.7%\\n- Memory SOL: 17.6%\\n- Efficiency: 92.7% (headroom: 7.3%)\\n- At Roofline: No\\n- Tensor Cores: Inactive\\n## BOTTLENECK ANALYSIS\\n### Category: COMPUTE\\nPre-computed: compute-bound kernel\\n\\n**Reasoning:** Compute utilization is very high (sm throughput 92.66%, compute SOL 92.7%) while DRAM/memory throughput is low (17.56%), matching roofline classification as compute-bound with only 7.3% headroom.\\n\\n**Root Cause:** Non-tensor-core execution path drives heavy vector ALU pressure for attention math.  Evidence: sm__pipe_tensor_cycles_active.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_active=0.0\\n**Recommended Fix:** Retarget the kernel to matrix-core/MFMA/Triton dot paths that map BF16 matmuls to hardware matrix units (or use a tuned FlashAttention backend that does). (Shifting QK/PV GEMM work off VALU increases effective compute throughput and reduces the current compute-pipe saturation.)\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n## PERFORMANCE TARGET\\n- PyTorch Eager baseline: 0.2918 ms\\n- Current best kernel: 0.9720 ms\\n- Target: Improve by at least 10% (< 0.8748 ms)\\n- Maintain numerical correctness (atol=1e-4 or rtol=1e-4)\\n- Preserve public API (same inputs/outputs, shapes, dtypes)\\n\\n## REQUIREMENTS\\n1. Apply the recommended fixes above to address the COMPUTE bottleneck\\n2. The implementation must be a complete, valid Python file\\n3. Main function must be named 'kernel_function' wrapping the Triton kernel\\n4. Keep the wrapper free of PyTorch compute primitives\\n\\n## OUTPUT FORMAT\\nOutput complete optimized kernel code in ```python blocks.\\nInclude only: imports, Triton kernel (@triton.jit), wrapper function (kernel_function).\\nNo testing code, benchmarks, or explanatory comments.\\n\\nGenerate the complete optimized kernel implementation:\"}]}],\"max_output_tokens\":24576,\"model\":\"gpt-5.3-codex\"}"}}, "request_meta": {"model": "gpt-5.3-codex", "max_output_tokens": 24576}, "response": {"http_version": "HTTP/1.1", "headers": [["Date", "Mon, 23 Mar 2026 03:28:13 GMT"], ["Content-Type", "application/json"], ["Transfer-Encoding", "chunked"], ["Connection", "keep-alive"], ["Server", "cloudflare"], ["x-ratelimit-limit-requests", "15000"], ["x-ratelimit-limit-tokens", "40000000"], ["x-ratelimit-remaining-requests", "14999"], ["x-ratelimit-remaining-tokens", "39998822"], ["x-ratelimit-reset-requests", "4ms"], ["x-ratelimit-reset-tokens", "1ms"], ["openai-version", "2020-10-01"], ["openai-organization", "user-1cxdgrbvyzsglmmbqabhwk1k"], ["openai-project", "proj_XNNf74ZO7x4HoDwE8wx7GRzr"], ["x-request-id", "req_ece7519d8fe54707b09f2f81c862e499"], ["openai-processing-ms", "14172"], ["cf-cache-status", "DYNAMIC"], ["X-Content-Type-Options", "nosniff"], ["Strict-Transport-Security", "max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload"], ["Content-Encoding", "gzip"], ["CF-RAY", "9e0a57eb5dcfe95e-